  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Contextualised background information",
      "text": "- external pageTaylor &amp; Francis: Russia’s war in Ukraine – resources, commentary, analysis and insightscall\\_made\n\n- external pageJSTOR Daily – where news meets its scholarly matchcall\\_made\n\n- external pageDe Gruyter free accesscall\\_made\n\n- external pageProQuest E-book Central: Ukraine and Russiacall\\_made\n\nDo you follow the events unfolding in Ukraine in the mainstream media but would like to read more about the background of the long-term processes involved and the historical context of this war of aggression? In addition to the daily news, our links lead you to well-researched, freely available content that will help you understand the bigger picture."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Contextualised background information",
      "text": "To help you make sense of the complexity surrounding this conflict, several publishers have curated reading lists of e-books and journal articles that elucidate the political and historical backgrounds of the war and put the current developments in context."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The ETH Library reading list",
      "text": "All full-text e-books are also available in our Ukraine and Russia collection. The titles listed here will be available to you until 30 June 2022. The list is updated continuously.\n\nIf you have any questions, please email ."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Staffnet",
      "text": "More than just data – Benefit from know-how #KnowMore – The prepared content issued by the ETH Library is at your free disposal and gives you a head start."
    }
  ],
